---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import data from '../../../data/generated/ca-5gc-sim.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const href = (value: string) => `${base.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}${value.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;
---
<SiteLayout title="ConnectionAgent documentation" lang="en" description="ConnectionAgent system architecture, reliability evaluation, and public component documentation.">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="home-kicker">ConnectionAgent · Documentation</div>
    <h1>Understand the system.<br />Evaluate reliability.</h1>
    <p>Explore the architecture of ConnectionAgent, how its reliability is evaluated, and the public interfaces and contracts owned by individual components. Start with the system view, then dive into component references.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a href={href('/en/architecture/system/')}>Read the system architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>Explore Benchmark <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <p>New to CA? These documents provide a guided path through the system.</p>
    <div class="reading-list">
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/architecture/system/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">01</span>
        <span><strong>System architecture and responsibility boundaries</strong><small>See how Agent Hosts, Runtime, Providers, environments, and Lab work together—and who owns authoritative state.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">02</span>
        <span><strong>Benchmark evaluation model</strong><small>Understand evaluation assets, frozen tasks, execution attempts, evidence validity, and final adjudication.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/architecture/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">03</span>
        <span><strong>Documentation sources and governance</strong><small>Learn why components own their public source declarations and how ca-docs synchronizes and publishes them.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Component reference</h2>
    <p>Global documents explain how the system fits together; component references describe public interfaces, readable state, and operations.</p>
    <table class="component-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Public reference</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/')}>ca-5gc-sim</a></td>
          <td>5GC simulation environment and related capabilities</td>
          <td><a href={href('/en/api/')}>API</a> · <a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/facts/')}>Facts ({data.counts.facts})</a> · <a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/operations/')}>Operations ({data.counts.operations})</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/tool-common/')}>tool-common</a></td>
          <td>Subject Identity and shared tool contracts</td>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/tool-common/')}>Component overview</a></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="home-footnote">The component index grows as owner repositories publish their public documentation manifests. Not every repository or capability is integrated yet.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>About this documentation</h2>
    <p>CA Docs owns cross-repository explanations, navigation, and public snapshots. Machine contracts, implementation behavior, and domain facts remain authoritative in their owner repositories. Each snapshot records its source revision for traceability.</p>
    <p><a href={href('/en/architecture/')}>Read about documentation governance and source synchronization →</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
